DESCRIPTION:45–50 min open-water swim at Malta coast\, 1\,500–1\,800m a
 t easy 2:35–2:40/100m — this replaces the long run entirely\; use the 
 session to practice sighting\, drafting position\, and steady pacing rathe
 r than hitting a distance target.\n\nReason: With the Half Oceanman as the
  nearest A-race and running still constrained by fatigue\, substituting a 
 second weekly OW swim accelerates swim-specific adaptation without adding 
 run injury risk.\n\nAI coaching 2026-08-01
