 rm-up\, 3×600m @ 2:22–2:
DESCRIPTION:60 min pool session: 2\,500m — 400m warm-up\, 3×600m @ 2:22
 –2:25/100m with 25-sec rest\, 400m pull-buoy cool-down at relaxed pace\;
  if splits drift beyond 2:30/100m on rep 2–3\, shorten to 2×600m and ad
 d an extra 200m drill set.\n\nReason: Tightening the rest interval to 25 s
 econds and adding a split-based bail-out rule makes this set a more accura
 te Half Oceanman race simulation while preventing over-reaching if fitness
  is still building.\n\nAI coaching 2026-08-01
